WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.190
A power station sends 20 megawatts along
cables with a total resistance of 5 ohms.

2
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.460
Send it at 25 kilovolts, and 16
per cent is wasted in the cables.

3
00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:17.470
Send it at 400 kilovolts, and the
waste drops to just 0.06 per cent.

4
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.660
Transformers make that possible:
two coils on an iron core,

5
00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.540
and no moving parts.

6
00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.010
So how does it change the voltage?

7
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.120
In this mission, you'll find what the
turns on each coil have to do with it.

8
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:33.320
Then you'll see why real
transformers waste energy,

9
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:36.930
and why the core is built
from thin, insulated sheets.

10
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:42.190
Your mission: explain how a transformer
changes a voltage with no moving parts.
